        "text": {
            "description_html": "<b>Emtek 8450-SB, Sandcast Bronze Single Cylinder Regular Deadbolt</b>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nThe Regular Sandcast Bronze Single Cylinder Deadbolt is a great way to add a touch of the old world to your doors without it looking ancient. This Regular Deadbolt manages to look all at once traditional and contemporary, in a beautiful blending of the old and new. It will fit doors with 2-3/4 inch or 2-3/8 inch backsets with thicknesses ranging from 1-3/8 inches to 3 inches. This is a single cylinder deadbolt so the latch is thrown and retracted by a thumb turn on the interior and by a key from the exterior. \r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nSandcasting is a process for casting metal in sand molds. The mold is made by packing the sand around a pattern. Molten bronze is then poured into a mold cavity formed out of sand. Each sand mold is used only once. The sand is then recycled for the next piece.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<b>Single Cylinder:</b> The deadbolt is thrown and retracted by a key from exterior and by a thumb turn from the interior\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nAlso Available Matching <a href=\"/products/regular-sandcast-bronze-double-cylinder-deadbolt-emtek-8350-sb\"><b>Double Cylinder Sandcast Bronze Deadbolt</b></a>\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<b>Features</b> of the Sandcast Bronze Regular Single Cylinder Deadbolt:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Keyway: Schlage C</li>\r\n<li>Solid bronze collar and rosette.</li>\r\n<li>Hardened steel bolt.</li>\r\n<li>Will fit standard 2-1/8\" door preparations.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<b>Specifications</b> of the Emtek Traditional Sandcast Bronze Deadbolt:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Exterior Diameter: 2-3/8\"</li>\r\n<li>Interior Diameter: 2-1/2\"</li>\r\n<li>Exterior Projection: 1\"</li>\r\n<li>Interior Projection: 1-1⁄4\"</li>\r\n<li>Door Thickness: 1-3/4\" to 3\"</li>\r\n<li>Backset: 2-3/8\" or 2-3/4\"</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0766/1489/3857/files/EMT-sandcast-finish.jpg?v=1704354510\" width=\"570\" height=\"191\" border=\"0\" alt=\"Emtek Finish Chart\">\r\n</p>",
